  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 157 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nThe beginning of the workweek will be pleasant as upper level flow \nturns zonal. Southerly surface winds will allow temperatures to \nsteadily rise throughout the week with temperatures increasing from \nlow to mid 40s on monday to low to upper 50s by Wednesday. Models \nsuggest the potential for two systems to watch towards midweek. The \nfirst is a weak shortwave midweek which could bring a quick chance \nfor rain. The second is towards the end of the week where recent \nguidance has suggested a trough off the west coast will develop into \na decent cut-off upper level low that tracks towards the Midwest. \nHowever, with this being a week out, a lot of discrepancies \nbetween models still exists and it will be something to keep an \neye on as details change with additional guidance.",
